# What may not enter an image's build context.
#
# `deployment-operations`: *"artifacts SHALL be free of environment-specific
# values, so that inspecting an artifact reveals nothing about where it is
# running"*. The two `Dockerfile`s declare no setting and copy no `.env` — but
# the web image copies a whole directory (`COPY apps/cybercanon/web ./`), and
# SvelteKit reads a `.env` sitting in it **at build time**. So a developer's
# local `.env` would be baked into a promoted artifact by a build that changed
# nothing and said nothing, and the same image would then carry one
# environment's address into every other.
#
# This file is what makes that impossible rather than unlikely, and
# `tests/tooling/test_container_artifacts.py` reads it: a path that is
# environment-specific, machine-specific or already built has to be matched
# here, or the build is refused a property it claims.

# Environment-specific values, wherever they are.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.npmrc.local

# Machine state: none of it is the revision being built.
.git
.github
.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.complexipy_cache
**/.import_linter_cache
**/.coverage
**/.DS_Store

# Already built here. An image builds from source, or it is reproducing a
# developer's machine rather than a revision.
**/.svelte-kit
apps/cybercanon/web/build
reports
